# Fail-closed integrations

```ts
// BAD — silent fake
catch { return { multiplier: 4, price: 234.01 }; }

// GOOD — labeled failure
catch (e) {
  return { ok: false as const, mode: "unavailable", reason: "xstocks_multiplier_fetch_failed", detail: String(e) };
}
```

- Every adapter returns `{ ok, mode, ... }` where mode ∈ `mainnet-read | quote-only | fork | paper | unavailable`.
- UI must show mode badges; never imply a broadcast fill from a quote.
- Yahoo/underlying prices ≠ xStock economic truth — use xStocks API + Pyth for desk truth.
- If Bitquery key missing, wash gate blocks size (fail-closed), does not invent "green".